From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:27:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: the SD reader's card
 detect

The J604's SD reader reports its card detect through the SMC's gP09
(Apple device tree pcie-sdreader: interrupt-parent smc-pmu, interrupts
<9>, card-detect-polarity 1). Describe it on the reader's root port and
let the SMC GPIO node offer interrupts. Nothing uses the line unless
pcie_apple.t8132_sd_port_off is set.

The level read with a card in and out is to be confirmed on the machine;
active high follows the Apple device tree's polarity of 1.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 508cb4a3c3..4b218e4827 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -312,10 +312,18 @@ &bluetooth0 {
 
 /*
  * The SD card reader, a GL9755 (ADT pci-bridge2/pcie-sdreader), powered by
- * the SMC's gP19 (function-sd_pwr_en).
+ * the SMC's gP19 (function-sd_pwr_en). Its card detect is the SMC's gP09
+ * (ADT pcie-sdreader: interrupt-parent smc-pmu, interrupts <9>,
+ * card-detect-polarity 1), which reports a card while the reader is off.
  */
 &port02 {
 	pwren-gpios = <&smc_gpio 0x19 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+	card-detect-gpios = <&smc_gpio 0x09 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+};
+
+&smc_gpio {
+	interrupt-controller;
+	#interrupt-cells = <2>;
 };
 
